WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.500
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:09.010
I take you, for better, for worse, for richer,
for poorer, in sickness and in health, to

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:14.720
love and to cherish, til death us do part…
or not.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:20.730
What if death wasn’t the end of marriage,
well for hundreds of French people every year,

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.210
it’s not.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.860
Necrogamy is the act of marrying the dead.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:31.710
It’s been legal to marry the deceased in
France since 1959 and every year in France

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:37.950
hundreds of ceremonies are held to marry an
individual with a deceased significant other.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:44.570
Whilst not as common, posthumous marriage
are also practiced in the US, Germany, Sudan,

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:48.320
Thailand, China, South Africa and South Korea.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.090
It’s easy to see why people who have tragically
lost their soul mate would want to do this,

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:56.200
it’s a beautiful symbolic gesture.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.149
Very odd but beautiful.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:04.140
But guys, what if quite the opposite happens,
what if you get sick of your wife?

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.799
And I don’t mean like that time when you
had to take a sabbatical in the garden shed

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:08.889
for two hours.

00:01:08.889 --> 00:01:12.530
I’m taking about actually selling your wife.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.579
Now before you go and list your beloved on
eBay just hold on a minute because it’s

00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:21.719
a little more complicated than that, not to
mention illegal, and you’ll just end up

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:25.780
with a slap to the face and a few more hours
in the shed.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:31.009
Wife-selling is not just an urban myth, it’s
a very real part of global history, particularly

00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:32.009
in old England.

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:37.829
Although, it is frowned upon today and rightfully
so, throughout some periods in history, wife-selling

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:39.460
was incredibly popular.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:45.099
So then, let’s go shopping, at an 19th century
market in Britain.

00:01:45.099 --> 00:01:50.020
A Victorian-era English market was a feast
for the senses.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:55.909
The smell of freshly roasted ham and coffee
beans tussled with the ghastly essence of

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:59.939
animal and even human sewage, running down
the street.

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:05.270
The sound of cattle and squealing pigs, pervade
the air, as did the chatter from the crowd,

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:10.319
brimming with vagabonds, thieves, the wealthy
and the not-so-wealthy.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:16.670
All of whom had to compete with street hawkers
selling their once most-prized possession,

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:17.670
their wives.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:23.590
“Roll up, roll up, she’s hard-working,
deceptively strong, and younger than she looks.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.459
Only 5 shillings, a real bargain folks.”

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:31.969
Men selling their wives was a common sight
at markets in Britain.

00:02:31.969 --> 00:02:37.870
Beginning in the late 17th century this common
practice continued all the way until the early

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.530
20th century.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:45.510
The first Court of Divorce was established
in England in 1857, before this it was very

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:50.890
costly and difficult to detangle oneself from
their wife.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:55.890
If a man wanted rid of his wife, or visa-versa,
the man would have to pay the present-day

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:02.659
equivalent of £15,000 for a private act of
parliament and you had to obtain the blessing

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:07.010
of the church, which was about as easy as
splitting an atom with a sledgehammer.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:12.939
So unsurprisingly, poorer members of society,
especially those who had large debts would

00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:16.500
look to sell their wives instead.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.480
Wife-selling was particularly popular in the
West Midlands of England, but Yorkshire held

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:28.420
the crown with the most number of Wife sales
between 1760 and 1880, and the only place

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:32.659
where a man would probably still trade his
wife for a pie today.

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:38.629
Men would sell their wives usually to pay
taxes they otherwise couldn’t afford, to

00:03:38.629 --> 00:03:43.170
settle gambling debts or to simply buy food
in times of famine.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:49.090
Now obviously being sold as a chattel isn’t
exactly nice but more often than not, the

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:54.050
decision wasn’t forced upon the wife and
a lot of the time it would be the woman’s

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.989
idea to be sold in the first place.

00:03:55.989 --> 00:04:01.359
If a marriage went sour and a couple were
no longer happy together it often made more

00:04:01.359 --> 00:04:06.799
sense for the woman to be sold and at least
she could be with someone else, rather than

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:11.049
continue their deeply unhappy relationship,
even if she didn’t see any of the profits

00:04:11.049 --> 00:04:12.760
from her sale.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:18.910
Regular divorce was just financially out of
the question for the vast majority of people.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.460
So the decision has been made, the wife’s
gotta go.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:26.229
But how exactly does a man go about selling
a person?

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:28.270
His own wife nonetheless!

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:34.970
Well there was actually a semi-official system
for doing so and it was surprisingly simple.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:40.220
The man would take his wife to the market
with a halter around her neck, just as he

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.550
would one of his animals.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.010
Shocking, I know.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.380
He would then have to pay a small “Market
Toll” which would allow him to sell goods

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.280
at the market that day.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.349
The rest was simply a matter of good sales
chatter.

00:04:52.349 --> 00:04:57.830
He would parade his misses around on a leash,
bellowing her “benefits” and “features”

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.849
from the top of his lungs.

00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:05.910
When he gathered a crowd of a few interested
punters, the auction would begin.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:11.130
Auctions usually started at a few pence but
could rise all the way up to one pound, yes

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:16.960
a pound, depending on how desirable the auctioneer’s
fair lady was.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:22.240
There may still be small inequality issues
in society today, but it’s fair to say we’ve

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.300
come a long, long way from the days when you
could tie your wife up like a pig, take her

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.050
to market and flog her for a pound.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:35.039
However, women weren’t simply offered to
the highest bidder, she had the option to

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:41.750
veto offers at her will, if she didn’t like
the look, or smell of the gentleman in question.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:46.770
Once a winning bidder had been found the exchange
would take place, which was basically a mini

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:53.919
marriage ceremony on the street, or often
in the pub, right there and then.

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:59.699
Before the Marriage Act of 1753 in England
a marriage did not require a formal ceremony

00:05:59.699 --> 00:06:01.199
with a vicar.

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:04.970
Marriage was no more than an agreement between
two people.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:10.020
Even after the marriage act came into effect
these quick street marriages still took place

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:15.819
but the church refused to recognise the couple’s
union, but that didn’t stop people.

00:06:15.819 --> 00:06:21.210
Astonishingly money wasn’t the only commodity
exchanged for a man’s wife.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:26.879
Here’s an actual snippet from the World
newspaper on November 12, 1790…

00:06:26.879 --> 00:06:32.849
“A man at Nimfield stocks in Sussex last
week sold his wife to another man of the same

00:06:32.849 --> 00:06:38.580
place for half a pint of gin; the purchaser
being in liquor at the time the bargain was

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.430
concluded, the seller in order that he should
not complain of any unfair advantage having

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:48.190
been taken of him took his dear spouse to
bed and board until the next morning when

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:52.960
the buyer attended and claimed his lady who
was delivered by the husband in due form,

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.300
having a halter round her neck, and two witnesses
being present.&nbsp;

00:06:56.300 --> 00:07:09.620
The woman appeared overjoyed at the change,
nor did the man seem less happy at their lots.”

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:15.561
After an exchange the now ex-husband handed
over a toll ticket, basically a receipt, to

00:07:15.561 --> 00:07:18.590
the new husband as a proof of sale.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:23.470
The act of wife-selling was slowly phased-out,
until it became completely unheard of by the

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.479
mid 20th century.

00:07:25.479 --> 00:07:28.470
As divorce courts became more prevalent and
cheaper.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:34.689
Well, in England at least, however wife-selling
remained a thing for many years, in a few

00:07:34.689 --> 00:07:38.990
other countries, even if most of the time
it was illegal.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:43.720
Today though, there is only one remaining
country that commonly practices wife-selling,

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:44.720
India.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:52.879
In rural India, particularly a region known
as Bundelkhand, life rests on that year’s

00:07:52.879 --> 00:07:53.879
harvest.

00:07:53.879 --> 00:07:57.560
If the harvest is poor then a famine is guaranteed.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:03.879
In times of desperation and starvation many
families turn to the local Paisawalla, a wealthy

00:08:03.879 --> 00:08:05.770
man who lends money.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:10.800
The local Paisawalla will loan farmers money
but the loans come with extremely high interest

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:11.800
rates.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:17.439
If the years ahead are also drought filled
and lead to poor harvests, then the farmer

00:08:17.439 --> 00:08:21.509
may not be able to sell crops and pay off
the expensive loan.

00:08:21.509 --> 00:08:27.289
In such situations they have but one option,
sell their wife.

00:08:27.289 --> 00:08:32.590
The farmer will either sell his wife to another
man and use the funds to pay off the Paisawalla,

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:38.090
or more often than not, the Paisawalla will
themself, take ownership of the man’s wife

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.570
and keep her as payment.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:46.680
Forcing her to live with him for as long as
the debt remains unpaid, even if that is forever.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:52.070
What’s even more sickening is that if the
Paisawalla believes the farmer’s wife is

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:57.190
not valuable enough to settle the debt in
full then he may take the farmer’s children

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:58.330
also.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:04.840
Sadly, this part of India is renowned for
its inhumane treatment of women.

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.880
But what about in the Western world?

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:10.900
Have there been any records of wife-selling
in the modern day?

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:17.100
Well unbelievably, yes, and it takes us back
to the historic home of wife-selling, Yorkshire.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:23.100
In 2016 a man from Wakefield, Yorkshire, listed
his long-term wife on eBay.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:28.651
After a long day at work the 33-year-old man
returned home to be subjected to his wife

00:09:28.651 --> 00:09:34.020
moaning at him, to which he replied “right
I’m going to put you up for sale.”

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:37.440
The listing was simply titled “Used Wife”.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.380
The description included the following…

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:45.290
“Good points: Body work and paint work still
in decent shape and has some skills in the

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.290
kitchen.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:51.640
Bad points: Often makes this noise that cannot
be silenced unless you order brand new shiny

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:52.760
parts of metal.”

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:58.000
And “Offers welcome, may consider a part
exchange for a younger model.”

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:04.100
The auction reached £65,000 before it was
removed by eBay.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:08.380
Thankfully it was just a joke and the couple
are still happily together.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:14.260
After he bought her many many shiny things
to say sorry.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:22.820
Thanks for watching.

